 "answer": "The flag is `--resume <evalId>`, for example `promptfoo eval --resume <evalId>`. It continues an interrupted or incomplete eval from its saved state, so you need the ID of the original run.\n\nPromptfoo also has `--retry-errors`, which re-runs only the tests that ended in an error. That's useful for failed tests but isn't the same as resuming a paused run.\n\nI'm not fully certain of these details, and CLI flags can change between versions, so check `promptfoo eval --help` for your installed version.",
